{"full":"hf:fffiloni/agentic-space-factory-UI-public","spaceId":"fffiloni/agentic-space-factory-UI-public","name":"Agentic Space Factory","source":"huggingface","description":"Build, inspect, validate Gradio Spaces from model cards.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":null,"topics":["docker","region:us"],"technologies":[],"likes":5,"created":"2026-06-16T15:39:27.000Z","updated":"2026-06-26T16:40:29.000Z","license":null,"runtime":"SLEEPING","appUrl":"https://fffiloni-agentic-space-factory-ui-public.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/fffiloni/agentic-space-factory-UI-public","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T23:44:22.935Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T23:44:22.935Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T23:44:22.935Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🏭","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Agentic Space Factory turns Hugging Face model cards into private, testable Gradio Spaces through an agentic build loop running on Hugging Face.","The app is an operator interface for model-to-Space generation. A user enters a model URL, reviews a compact pre-scan, launches a build, watches progress, opens the generated Space, validates the live API, and inspects the full run archive.","The project builds on the idea that a deployed Space can be the coding assistant's lab: generated code is not enough; the live Space must boot, expose an API, run inference, and return a valid artifact."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/fffiloni/agentic-space-factory-UI-public/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"ba2e743bf234e52d359d9f8a1675874d9e9e6a24803c866812886f967a2238fc","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T22:29:39.206Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T23:44:22.977Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Agentic Space Factory turns Hugging Face model cards into private, testable Gradio Spaces through an agentic build loop running on Hugging Face.","sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/fffiloni/